From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:52:28 +0200
Subject: media: uapi: add VC-1 stateless decoder pixel format
 and controls

Add the V4L2_PIX_FMT_VC1_SLICE pixel format and the compound controls
for stateless VC-1 decoders (SMPTE 421M Simple, Main and Advanced
profiles, also known as WMV3 and WVC1):

  V4L2_CID_STATELESS_VC1_SEQUENCE           sequence layer (STRUCT_C/A)
  V4L2_CID_STATELESS_VC1_ENTRYPOINT_HEADER  entry-point header
  V4L2_CID_STATELESS_VC1_PICTURE_LAYER      picture layer, references
  V4L2_CID_STATELESS_VC1_BITPLANES          decoded bitplanes
  V4L2_CID_STATELESS_VC1_SLICE_PARAMS       slice locations (dynamic array)

The API is frame based: a request decodes one coded picture, which is a
progressive frame, an interlaced frame or one field of a field
interlaced frame. The second field of a frame is decoded into the
capture buffer of the first one, as for MPEG-2 and H.264 field
pictures. An Advanced profile output buffer holds the picture with its
start codes and emulation prevention bytes, a Simple or Main profile
one holds the frame as carried by the container.

The controls carry the complete picture header state, the size of the
picture header so that hardware can start at the first macroblock, and
the bitplanes of the picture header in decoded form. Userspace has to
decode the bitplanes anyway to reach the syntax elements behind them,
and the kernel should not parse variable length codes. The slice
parameters are only exposed by drivers which need them, e.g. to learn
the length of the picture header which a slice repeats; such drivers
need them with every request.

Decoding a picture also depends on the state of its references which
is not in its own headers: their picture types, frame coding mode,
range reduction and the intensity compensation which the pictures
decoded since then applied to them. As for H.264 and HEVC, this is
passed with every request (struct v4l2_vc1_reference), so that drivers
don't have to remember anything from one request to the next.

Skipped pictures have no macroblock layer and are not queued: the
application repeats their reference picture. The capture buffer holds
the picture before the Main profile range expansion and the Advanced
profile range mapping, which SMPTE 421M specifies as output processes;
the application has their parameters. A reduced resolution (RESPIC)
picture is likewise stored at its coded size, in the top-left corner
of the capture buffer, and upsampling it is left to the application,
as SMPTE 421M leaves the upsampling filter to the implementation.
Pre-release WMV3 streams, whose
macroblock layer is coded differently, are flagged by the RES_RTM bit
of the sequence layer so that drivers can refuse them.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
[aiyengar: default VC-1 Sequence Layer is a conformant Simple profile
 (RES_RTM set) so that TRY_EXT_CTRLS of the default passes v4l2-compliance]
